import Googology.Trans.BMS.TrioRulesNonLast
import Googology.Trans.BMS.TrioRules2Sheet

/-!
# Fix N against the sheet, the order, BMS expansion and nearby ordinals

The checks of `TrioRules2Sheet.lean`, re-run for the rules with Fix N
(`TrioRulesNonLast.lean`), and the evidence for Fix N.

* **The sheet.**  On all 813 labels of
  [`tools/omega_alpha_rows.tsv`](https://github.com/koteitan/trio/blob/main/tools/omega_alpha_rows.tsv)
  and on the 9 corrected labels of [TRIO-SHEET-41.md](TRIO-SHEET-41.md), Fix N gives
  the matrix of `TrioRules2.lean`, so every `#guard` of `TrioRules2Sheet.lean`
  holds for it as well.
* **The order check** of `TrioRules2Sheet.lean`: the 783 chosen matrices are in the
  order of their labels (306,153 pairs, 0 disagreements).
* **Fix N on the plan's case**: `M(Ω_{Ω_Ω}+Ω_{Ω_2}+1)` is below `M(Ω_{Ω_Ω}·2)`
  (it was above), and the collisions are gone.
* **BMS expansion** (`expandRL 3 n`, BM4 expansion with `n + 1` copies of the
  bad part, as yaBMS `[n]`): the lifted copy is what BMS writes; the sheet's rows
  `Ω_Ω·ω` (4460) and `Ω_{Ω_Ω}·ω` (4748) expand onto Fix N's matrices, whose FS is
  cofinal; and the `·ω` of each new form expands onto the new forms.
* **Nearby ordinals**: two families of sums and products around `Ω_{Ω_Ω}` and
  `Ω_Ω`, and the 71 nearby ordinals of the `TrioRules2` report.

All of it is `#guard`s: a calibration, not a theorem.  (Standard form is checked
with yaBMS `bms -s` outside Lean; the numbers are in
[TRIO-NONLAST-LEAF.md](TRIO-NONLAST-LEAF.md).)
-/

namespace Googology.Trans.BMS.TrioRulesNL

open Googology.Trans.BMS.TrioRules
open Googology.Trans.BMS.TrioRules2
open Googology.Trans.BMS (expandRL)

/-- The matrix by the rules with Fix N (`[]` when the label does not parse). -/
def nOf (s : String) : List (List Nat) := (trioRuleMatrixOfN s).getD []

/-- The matrix by `TrioRules2.lean`. -/
def oOf (s : String) : List (List Nat) := (trioRuleMatrixOf2 s).getD []

