/-! ### The lifted copy is BMS's own

`M(Ω_{Ω_Ω}+Ω_{Ω_ω})[1]` and `M(Ω_{Ω_Ω}+Ω_ω)[1]` (both marks of `TrioRules2.lean`;
`+Ω_ω` is row 4743) are the matrix before the mark followed by `blift` from the
leaf's row-1 parent, with the leaf lifted (`Ω_{Ω_3}`, `Ω_3`).  Fix N's copy is the
same with the leaf kept. -/

/-- `blift` with the leaf lifted instead of kept. -/
def bliftUp (cs : Cols) (s0 : Nat) : Cols :=
  let seg := blift cs s0
  setLastY seg ((lastC seg).y + 1)

